# AN N-ARY CHAIN DECOMPOSED OVER INDIVIDUALS (SPEC 5.3 L2, L6). r1 ∘ r2 ∘ r3 ⊑ t
# is decomposed left-associated through a fresh role; the asserted r1(a,b),
# r2(b,c), r3(c,d) must compose into t(a,d). domain(t) = F makes a an F; G(a),
# F disjoint from G. Expect: INCONSISTENT (exit 1).

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:F a owl:Class . :G a owl:Class . :F owl:disjointWith :G .
:r1 a owl:ObjectProperty . :r2 a owl:ObjectProperty . :r3 a owl:ObjectProperty .
:t a owl:ObjectProperty .
:t owl:propertyChainAxiom ( :r1 :r2 :r3 ) .
:t rdfs:domain :F .
:a a owl:NamedIndividual , :G . :b a owl:NamedIndividual .
:c a owl:NamedIndividual . :d a owl:NamedIndividual .
:a :r1 :b . :b :r2 :c . :c :r3 :d .
